<comment datatype='string'>Thermobifida fusca B6 is an engineered strain of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-2021&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Thermobifida fusca&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; constructed to produce &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=PROPANOL&quot;&gt;propan-1-ol&lt;/a&gt;. The native &lt;i&gt;celR&lt;/i&gt; gene (encoding &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-3.2.1.4&quot;&gt;EC 3.2.1.4, cellulase&lt;/a&gt;) was replaced by &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-12174&quot;&gt;adhE2&lt;/a&gt;, a bifunctional butyryl aldehyde/butanol dehydrogenase gene from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1488&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium acetobutylicum&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21757023&quot;&gt;Deng11&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26227414&quot;&gt;Deng15b&lt;/a&gt;]. The strain was later shown to produce and accumulate &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=ADIPATE&quot;&gt;adipate&lt;/a&gt; [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26189483&quot;&gt;Deng15a&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
